      "writtenOn": "2026-06-29T19:32:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I realize now that we can\u0027t quite use the public `drawEdgeAAQuad` API here because it is restricting things to only a color and a blend-mode (but technically what should be included is any SkColorFilter and the option for an SkBlender).\n\nThere aren\u0027t any underlying limitations that prevent us from creating the EdgeAAQuad geometry and calling `drawGeometry` with a PaintParams created from the paint.  I think it would be reasonable to add another constructor to PaintParams that mirrors the SimpleImage override version, like `PaintParams(const SkPaint\u0026, const SkColor4f\u0026 colorOverride); // multiplies with paint\u0027s alpha`.\n\nIn this paint override, since we\u0027re taking in an SkColor4f (so the drawImageLattice code lifts its `nextFixedColor` to float before hand, the alpha multiply is trivial inside the PaintParams ctor.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 999,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 1000,
        "endChar": 89
      },
      "revId": "5fa6e2c1160ca6482c58a5b881b47dbd8b5e5572",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
